('baf87e1a-d705-41aa-a641-f9f7837c7d41', 'Israeli army launches more air strikes as truce violations continue', '<p>The Israeli prime minister has spoken on the phone with Russian President Vladimir Putin, reports Russian state media, citing the Kremlin.</p><p>The two leaders discussed the ceasefire in Gaza, Iran’s nuclear programme, and efforts to “promote further stabilisation in Syria”, according to the TASS news agency.</p><p>Lawyers have heard harrowing accounts of abuse and torture from Palestinians held in a notorious Israeli prison.</p><p>Dozens of Palestinian and Lebanese nationals are detained in the Rakevet facility below the Nitzan prison in Ramla, which was closed in the 1980s after conditions were deemed inhumane.</p><p>Israel’s national security minister has posted several videos from that facility and other jails, boasting about the cruelties inflicted on the prisoners.</p><p>The Israeli prime minister has spoken on the phone with Russian President Vladimir Putin, reports Russian state media, citing the Kremlin.</p><p>The two leaders discussed the ceasefire in Gaza, Iran’s nuclear programme, and efforts to “promote further stabilisation in Syria”, according to the TASS news agency.</p><p>Lawyers have heard harrowing accounts of abuse and torture from Palestinians held in a notorious Israeli prison.</p><p>Dozens of Palestinian and Lebanese nationals are detained in the Rakevet facility below the Nitzan prison in Ramla, which was closed in the 1980s after conditions were deemed inhumane.</p><p>Israel’s national security minister has posted several videos from that facility and other jails, boasting about the cruelties inflicted on the prisoners.</p><p>The Israeli prime minister has spoken on the phone with Russian President Vladimir Putin, reports Russian state media, citing the Kremlin.</p><p>The two leaders discussed the ceasefire in Gaza, Iran’s nuclear programme, and efforts to “promote further stabilisation in Syria”, according to the TASS news agency.</p><p>Lawyers have heard harrowing accounts of abuse and torture from Palestinians held in a notorious Israeli prison.</p><p>Dozens of Palestinian and Lebanese nationals are detained in the Rakevet facility below the Nitzan prison in Ramla, which was closed in the 1980s after conditions were deemed inhumane.</p><p>Israel’s national security minister has posted several videos from that facility and other jails, boasting about the cruelties inflicted on the prisoners.</p>', 'cbaa2e37-3e41-4943-9de7-e6d525ccecec', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'No', '1763232968_a71bd6d27320d121a9e7.webp', '2025-11-15 18:56:08.196970', '2025-11-19 03:59:17.792310', NULL),
('0b8f699f-8ae9-4fcf-ba93-62917a9000cd', 'Trump says he is designating Saudi Arabia as a major non-NATO ally', '<p>President Donald Trump said Tuesday that the United States will designate Saudi Arabia as a major non-NATO ally, announcing the decision during a black-tie dinner at the White House with Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman.</p><p>“I’m pleased to announce that we’re taking our military cooperation to even greater heights by formally designating Saudi Arabia as a major non-NATO ally, which is something that is very important to them,” the president said.</p><p>“And I’m just telling you now for the first time, because I wanted to keep a little secret for tonight, and just heard him say, ‘Oh, that’s nice,’” Trump added.</p><p>Trump’s announcement underscores a push by the United States to deepen and formalize its military partnership with the kingdom. He said earlier Tuesday that Saudi Arabia&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/11/18/middleeast/f35-trump-saudi-arabia-israel-latam-intl\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>will purchase F-35 fighter jets</strong></a>&nbsp;it’s long coveted.</p><p>Trump and the crown prince also finalized “a series of landmark agreements that deepen the U.S.-Saudi strategic partnership, expand opportunities for high-paying American jobs, strengthen critical supply chains, and reinforce regional stability,” according to the White House.</p><p>Speaking at the dinner, Crown Prince bin Salman touted his kingdom’s relationship with the US, saying, “today is a special day.”</p><p>“We’ve been signing a lot of agreement that’s going to open the door to develop the relation deeper in many areas,” he said.</p><p><strong>Major non-NATO ally:&nbsp;</strong>Major non-NATO allies are not entitled to specific security guarantees, like NATO members under Article 5, but the designation changes how the US military interacts with the country, according to the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.state.gov/major-non-nato-ally-status/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>State Department</strong></a>.</p><p>These allies are eligible to receive material and supply loans, serve as a location for US-owned War Reserve stockpiles and can enter into agreements with the United States on training. Additionally, private companies from the designated country can bid on contracts to maintain, repair or overhaul US military equipment overseas. Currently, 19 countries are designated as major non-NATO allies, including Israel, Japan and New Zealand.</p>', 'cf5e983b-3e96-4d99-803c-94b120cbae05', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'No', '1763526059_b8d38a2dcfe858e96a69.png', '2025-11-19 04:21:00.741291', '2025-11-19 05:20:14.866615', NULL);
INSERT INTO `news` (`newsid`, `title`, `content`, `categoryid`, `status`, `posted_by`, `breaking_news`, `cover_picture`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
('77abed4e-4eea-4dee-be77-f7bf84544a54', 'President and first lady welcome Saudi crown prince back to the White House for a black-tie dinner', '<p>Saudi Arabia’s Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman returned to the White House on Tuesday evening for a black-tie dinner, capping a day of high-level diplomacy that included an&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/11/18/politics/khashoggi-murder-trump-bin-saudi-crown-prince\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>Oval Office meeting</strong></a>&nbsp;and bilateral lunch with President Donald Trump.</p><p>Trump, dressed in a black tuxedo, and first lady Melania Trump, wearing an emerald gown, greeted the crown prince at the South Lawn entrance as a military band stood at attention, marking a ceremonial welcome underscoring the significance of the visit.</p><p>The guest list includes largely chief executives, as well as lawmakers and governors — some of whom Trump himself called to invite to the dinner, people familiar with the plans&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/11/16/politics/saudi-crown-prince-trump-white-house\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>previously told CNN</strong></a>. The event is being coordinated by Melania Trump, as all state visits are planned through the first lady’s office.</p><p>While the White House has decided to pull out all the stops, the visit cannot be classified as an official state visit as Prince bin Salman is not Saudi Arabia’s head of state. That position is occupied by his 89-year-old father,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2015/01/23/middleeast/who-is-saudi-arabia-king-salman\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>King Salman</strong></a>. But the crown prince has assumed almost all day-to-day responsibility for ruling the kingdom, and attends summits and other diplomatic engagements as the country’s leader.</p><p><br></p><p>House Oversight Chair James Comer highlighted an email Democratic fundraisers sent to Jeffrey Epstein on behalf of Hakeem Jeffries in 2013 as part of a broader accusation that Democrats were cherry-picking information in the files from the convicted sex offender’s estate to selectively criticize President Donald Trump.</p><p>“Another email shows Democrat fundraisers invited Epstein to an event or to meet privately with Hakeem Jeffries as part of their 2013 effort to win a majority. So Hakeem Jeffries’ campaign solicited money from Jeffrey Epstein. That’s what we found in the last document batch,” Comer said on the House floor on Tuesday.</p><p>A Democratic consulting group asked Epstein in a March 2013 email if he wanted to participate in a fundraising dinner with Jeffries and former President Barack Obama or get to know Jeffries better.</p><p>“Sometimes referred to as ‘Brooklyn’s Barack,’ he is a staunch supporter of President Obama and a progressive voice for the people of New York City,” the email from Dynamic SRG reads.</p><p>There is no evidence Epstein responded. CNN has reached out to Dynamic SRG for comment. A Jeffries spokesperson pointed to FEC filings, which show the consulting group has not worked with Jeffries since 2015. And there is no&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.fec.gov/data/receipts/individual-contributions/?contributor_name=Epstein%2C+Jeff&amp;two_year_transaction_period=2014\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>record</strong></a>&nbsp;of Epstein giving Jeffries money directly.</p><p class=\"ql-align-right\"><br></p><p><br></p>', 'cf5e983b-3e96-4d99-803c-94b120cbae05', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'Yes', '1763529118_8ff3f9238100c7eefd64.png', '2025-11-19 05:11:58.917928', '2025-11-19 05:12:33.270905', NULL),
('92a212ee-b5c7-404b-a5b8-e1035b414196', 'Election Center 2025', '<h1><strong>Election Center 2025</strong></h1><p>In the first major electoral test of the second Trump administration, Democrats swept the major races in Virginia, New Jersey and New York City, while voters in California approved a new congressional map that could help Democrats win five more House seats next year.</p><p>In the first major electoral test of the second Trump administration, Democrats swept the major races in Virginia, New Jersey and New York City, while voters in California approved a new congressional map that could help Democrats win five more House seats next year.</p><p>In the first major electoral test of the second Trump administration, Democrats swept the major races in Virginia, New Jersey and New York City, while voters in California approved a new congressional map that could help Democrats win five more House seats next year.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li><br></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p>', '147b4f6c-5a01-48d0-b45e-925d23f0612b', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'Yes', '1763529749_9b21a39177a6ed2f163e.png', '2025-11-19 05:22:29.156283', '2025-11-19 05:23:46.207715', NULL),
('ddd25aaf-9347-492d-b8dc-1ffcbfb097b7', 'Takeaways from Tuesday’s elections: Democrats win across the spectrum as voters reject Trump', '<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Video provides a powerful way to help you prove your point. When you click Online Video, you can paste in the embed code for the video you want to add. You can also type a keyword to search online for the video that best fits your document.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">To make your document look professionally produced, Word provides header, footer, cover page, and text box designs that complement each other. For example, you can add a matching cover page, header, and sidebar. Click Insert and then choose the elements you want from the different galleries.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Themes and styles also help keep your document coordinated. When you click Design and choose a new Theme, the pictures, charts, and SmartArt graphics change to match your new theme. When you apply styles, your headings change to match the new theme.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Save time in Word with new buttons that show up where you need them. To change the way a picture fits in your document, click it and a button for layout options appears next to it. When you work on a table, click where you want to add a row or a column, and then click the plus sign.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Reading is easier, too, in the new Reading view. You can collapse parts of the document and focus on the text you want. If you need to stop reading before you reach the end, Word remembers where you left off - even on another device.</p><p><br></p>', '147b4f6c-5a01-48d0-b45e-925d23f0612b', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'Yes', '1763530241_0d2ffa6fb1e237ece103.jpg', '2025-11-19 05:30:41.090116', '2025-11-19 05:31:17.568006', NULL),
('10525f84-ce15-4a87-a29a-1c39e59596d0', 'Video provides a powerful way to help you prove your point', '<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Video provides a powerful way to help you prove your point. When you click Online Video, you can paste in the embed code for the video you want to add. You can also type a keyword to search online for the video that best fits your document.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">To make your document look professionally produced, Word provides header, footer, cover page, and text box designs that complement each other. For example, you can add a matching cover page, header, and sidebar. Click Insert and then choose the elements you want from the different galleries.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Themes and styles also help keep your document coordinated. When you click Design and choose a new Theme, the pictures, charts, and SmartArt graphics change to match your new theme. When you apply styles, your headings change to match the new theme.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Save time in Word with new buttons that show up where you need them. To change the way a picture fits in your document, click it and a button for layout options appears next to it. When you work on a table, click where you want to add a row or a column, and then click the plus sign.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Reading is easier, too, in the new Reading view. You can collapse parts of the document and focus on the text you want. If you need to stop reading before you reach the end, Word remembers where you left off - even on another device.</p><p><br></p>', 'cbaa2e37-3e41-4943-9de7-e6d525ccecec', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'Yes', '1763530477_d97b3d6241104c8e971b.jpg', '2025-11-19 05:34:37.344506', '2025-11-19 05:34:57.780443', NULL),
('35d75642-2721-45ee-a544-1503ffb9393d', 'Democrats win across the spectrum as voters reject Trump', '<p>Voters up and down the East Coast&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/election-news-11-04-25\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>delivered Democrats a sweep</strong></a>&nbsp;on Tuesday, electing candidates across the party’s ideological spectrum in a vivid show of discontent with President Donald Trump nearly a year into his second term.</p><p>In Virginia, moderate former Rep.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/11/04/politics/virginia-governor-abigail-spanberger-wins\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>Abigail Spanberger</strong></a>&nbsp;turned in the strongest Democratic performance in the state’s recent history as she coasted to victory. And in New Jersey, another moderate, Rep.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/11/04/politics/nj-governor-mikie-sherrill-wins\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>Mikie Sherrill</strong></a>, busted apart the coalition Trump and her Republican rival, former state lawmaker Jack Ciattarelli, had put together to close the Garden State’s gap in recent elections.</p><p>In New York City, democratic socialist&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/11/04/politics/nyc-mayor-zohran-mamdani-wins\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>Zohran Mamdani’s win</strong></a>&nbsp;marked the second time this year he’d defeated former Gov. Andrew Cuomo — first in the Democratic primary, and then in the general election, with Cuomo running as an independent backed by Trump.</p>', 'cf5e983b-3e96-4d99-803c-94b120cbae05', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'Yes', '1763530827_b10883a65a0555653381.png', '2025-11-19 05:40:27.672368', '2025-11-19 05:40:54.181763', NULL),
('8500bcca-2049-4e15-971e-5bdb3ab6c5fe', 'Sabiu Lawali Tsafe', '<p>Sabu</p>', '147b4f6c-5a01-48d0-b45e-925d23f0612b', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'No', '1763531025_c7f5397a3849114c21aa.jpg', '2025-11-19 05:43:45.495698', '2025-11-19 05:43:55.597094', NULL),
('dc6281cc-5b9b-4258-b223-3b7bd9ec1e78', 'TWG-GBV condemns attack on GGSS Maga, seeks urgent action', '<p>The Kebbi State Technical Working Group on Gender-Based Violence (TWG-GBV) has condemned the attack on Government Girls’ Secondary School, Maga, in the Zuru Emirate, which led to the death of a staff member, injury to a security officer and abduction of 25 female students.</p><p><br></p><p>Alhaji Nasiru Idris, Secretary of the TWG-GBV, made this known while briefing newsmen on behalf of the group on Friday in Birnin Kebbi.</p><p><br></p><p>He said the TWG-GBV, chaired by the First Lady of Kebbi State, Hajiya Zainab Nasare (Kauran Gwandu), described the incident as “tragic, unacceptable and a direct attack on the future of the Nigerian child”.</p><p><br></p><p>According to him, the Group expressed sympathy to the families, parents and the entire Zuru Emirate over the attack and abduction.</p><p><br></p><p>Idris said the TWG-GBV also acknowledged the immediate steps taken by Gov. Nasiru Idris and the First Lady, who have been mobilising security agencies and activating rescue operations to ensure the safe return of the 25 abducted students.</p><p><br></p><p>He said the Group called for urgent and coordinated action to support ongoing rescue efforts and strengthen security across schools in the state.</p><p><br></p><p>The secretary listed some of the immediate priority actions as strengthening security around schools, activating community early-warning systems, deploying specialised rescue and intelligence teams, and providing psychosocial support to affected families and students.</p><p><br></p><p>He added that the Group further recommended continuous communication with parents and guardians to reduce anxiety and curb misinformation.</p><p><br></p><p>On medium-term measures, Idris said the TWG-GBV urged government to upgrade physical and digital security infrastructure in schools, empower community vigilance groups, and consider converting the Zuru Airstrip and other strategic locations into Forward Operating Bases (FOBs) for enhanced surveillance.</p><p><br></p><p>He said the Group also advised the state to establish a Statewide Security Coordination and Response Framework to improve collaboration between security agencies, traditional rulers, faith leaders and community structures.</p><p><br></p><p>Idris said the TWG-GBV appealed to government to consider declaring a work-free day for statewide prayers and reflection in support of the safe return of the girls.</p><p><br></p><p>He urged residents to remain calm, vigilant and supportive of rescue operations, and to report any suspicious movement to relevant authorities.</p><p><br></p><p>“ The thoughts, prayers and solidarity of the TWG-GBV remain with the families of the abducted girls, the Zuru Emirate and the entire state,” the secretary said.</p>', 'cf5e983b-3e96-4d99-803c-94b120cbae05', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'Yes', '1763811717_83f3d2c618750f79f0dd.jpg', '2025-11-22 11:41:57.954845', '2025-11-22 11:45:07.512821', NULL),
('76acf6f4-2312-4bcf-a6f4-02fbb957bbea', 'Zelensky warns of ‘difficult moment in history’ after Trump gives Ukraine days to accept his plan to end war', '<h2>US President Donald Trump has given Ukraine less than a week to accept his plan – widely seen as favoring Russia – to end the war, as President Volodymyr Zelensky said his country faced “one of the most difficult moments” in its history.“I’ve had a lot of deadlines, but if things are working well, you tend to extend the deadlines. But Thursday is it,” the US president said in a radio interview with Fox News.The 28-point plan put forward by Trump&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/11/21/politics/trump-ukraine-peace-gaza-witkoff\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>puts pressure</strong></a>&nbsp;on Kyiv to cede territory, limit the size of its military and promise not to join NATO in exchange for an end to the war, all long-standing Kremlin demands.It was characterized by Zelensky during a video address to the nation on Friday as presenting Ukraine with a choice between losing its dignity or a key ally.</h2><h2><br></h2><h2>US President Donald Trump has given Ukraine less than a week to accept his plan – widely seen as favoring Russia – to end the war, as President Volodymyr Zelensky said his country faced “one of the most difficult moments” in its history.“I’ve had a lot of deadlines, but if things are working well, you tend to extend the deadlines. But Thursday is it,” the US president said in a radio interview with Fox News. The 28-point plan put forward by Trump&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/11/21/politics/trump-ukraine-peace-gaza-witkoff\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(12, 12, 12);\"><strong>puts pressure</strong></a>&nbsp;on Kyiv to cede territory, limit the size of its military and promise not to join NATO in exchange for an end to the war, all long-standing Kremlin demands.It was characterized by Zelensky during a video address to the nation on Friday as presenting Ukraine with a choice between losing its dignity or a key ally.</h2><h2><br></h2><h2><br></h2><p><br></p>', 'cf5e983b-3e96-4d99-803c-94b120cbae05', 'published', '12345abcd54321', 'No', '1763812333_5081c39fa0e24688ff75.jpg', '2025-11-22 11:52:13.515330', '2025-11-22 11:53:03.953211', NULL);
